# Environment contract for Cellbreak — NAMES ONLY, NEVER VALUES.
#
# ── The whole contract is: there isn't one. ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The Worker reads NO environment variables at runtime. Not a database URL, not an API
# key, not an auth project id. That is not an oversight and it is not "not yet" — it is
# what the design bought:
#
#   * no database          rooms live in their own Durable Object and outlive nothing
#   * no accounts          a nickname and a room code, so nothing to authenticate against
#   * no third-party API   the game is the whole product
#
# Bindings — the assets directory and the ROOMS Durable Object namespace — are declared in
# `cellbreak/apps/server/wrangler.jsonc` and resolved by the platform, not by env vars.
#
# ⚠️ If you are about to add the first one, read docs/secrets.md BEFORE choosing where it
# lives. A project with zero secrets has no habits yet, and the first one sets them.
#
# The only credential in the project belongs to CI, never to the app:
#   CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN   GitHub Actions secret — lets `wrangler deploy` publish
#   CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID  GitHub Actions secret — not secret, but set the same way
#
# Both are documented in docs/secrets.md and docs/env-matrix.md. Neither is ever read by
# the running Worker, so neither belongs in a `.env` file on anyone's laptop.
